==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|NL.|en}} {{m|la|paraplegia}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|παραπληγία}}, Ionic Greek for {{m|grc|παραπληξία||paralysis on one side}}, from {{m|grc|παραπλήσσεσθαι||to be stricken on one side}}, active {{m|grc|παραπλήσσειν||to strike on one side}}, from {{m|grc|παρά||beside}} + {{m|grc|πλήσσειν||to strike}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} A [[condition]] where the lower half of a patient's body is [[paralyzed]] and cannot move.

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|monoplegia}}
* {{l|en|hemiplegia}}
* {{l|en|paraplegic}}
* {{l|en|quadriplegia}}

